    <h1>SITETRACK MASTER TERMS OF SERVICE (B2B SaaS)</h1>
    <p><strong>Last Updated:</strong> [Insert Date]</p>

    <p>This Master Terms of Service Agreement (the "Agreement") is entered into by and between [Insert Company Name] ABN [Insert ABN] (hereinafter referred to as "SiteTrack", "we", "us", or "our") and the business entity registering for the SiteTrack platform (hereinafter referred to as the "Customer", "you", or "your").</p>
    
    <p>By registering for an account, accessing, or using the SiteTrack software platform (the "Service"), you acknowledge that you have read, understood, and agree to be bound by this Agreement. If you do not agree to these terms, you must not access or use the Service.</p>

    <h2>1. PROVISION OF THE SERVICE & NATURE OF SOFTWARE</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">License Grant:</span> Subject to the terms of this Agreement and payment of all applicable fees, SiteTrack grants the Customer a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable, and revocable license to access and use the Service strictly for its internal business operations.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Not a Certifying Authority:</span> SiteTrack provides a digital software tool for data management. SiteTrack is <strong>NOT</strong> an engineering firm, fire safety certifying authority, or compliance regulatory body. SiteTrack does not verify the physical reality, accuracy, or legal compliance of any Customer Data.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">AS 1851-2012 Compliance:</span> The Customer holds sole responsibility for ensuring that all physical fire safety inspections, maintenance, reporting, and physical works comply with Australian Standard 1851-2012 and any other applicable legislation. Except where directly caused by a material defect in the SiteTrack platform software itself, SiteTrack shall bear no responsibility for any failure of fire protection systems, property damage, injury, death, or regulatory non-compliance resulting from the Customer's operations.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Service Level Availability (SLA):</span> We will use commercially reasonable efforts to ensure the Service is available 24 hours a day, 7 days a week. However, we do not guarantee uninterrupted uptime and reserve the right to perform scheduled maintenance with prior notice.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>2. CUSTOMER OBLIGATIONS</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Account Security:</span> The Customer is entirely responsible for maintaining the confidentiality of its login credentials.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Authorised Users:</span> The Customer guarantees that all Authorised Users are at least eighteen (18) years of age and hold the necessary valid professional licenses (e.g., FPAS accreditation) required to perform their duties.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>3. INTELLECTUAL PROPERTY & DATA OWNERSHIP</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">SiteTrack IP:</span> SiteTrack exclusively retains all rights, title, and interest in and to the Service, including all source code, design, trademarks, and underlying intellectual property. The Customer is granted only a right to use the Service as described herein.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Customer Data:</span> The Customer retains all rights, title, and interest in and to all data entered into the Service ("Customer Data"). The Customer grants SiteTrack a worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive license to host, copy, transmit, and display Customer Data solely as necessary to provide the Service.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Sub-processors:</span> SiteTrack may use third-party sub-processors (e.g., cloud hosting providers) to provide the Service. SiteTrack will maintain a list of current sub-processors and notify the Customer of any material changes.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>4. FEES AND PAYMENT</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Subscription Fees:</span> The Customer agrees to pay all fees associated with their chosen subscription plan. SiteTrack reserves the right to suspend access if payment is overdue.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>5. DISCLAIMER & AUSTRALIAN CONSUMER LAW</h2>
    <p>Nothing in this Agreement excludes, restricts, or modifies any consumer guarantee, right, or remedy under the Australian Consumer Law (ACL) that cannot lawfully be excluded, restricted, or modified.</p>
    <p class="all-caps">Subject to the above, the Service is provided strictly on an "AS IS" and "AS AVAILABLE" basis. SiteTrack expressly disclaims all warranties of any kind, whether express or implied, including the implied warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose.</p>

    <h2>6. MUTUAL INDEMNIFICATION</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Customer Indemnity:</span> The Customer agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless SiteTrack from and against third-party claims arising from (a) the Customer's breach of AS 1851-2012, (b) property damage, personal injury, or death resulting from the Customer's faulty physical fire safety work, except to the extent caused by SiteTrack's gross negligence or material software defect.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">SiteTrack Indemnity:</span> SiteTrack agrees to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless the Customer from and against third-party claims arising from (a) infringement of third-party intellectual property rights by the SiteTrack platform, or (b) a data breach directly caused by SiteTrack's gross negligence.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>7. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY</h2>
    <p class="all-caps">To the maximum extent permitted by law, neither party shall be liable for any indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, including loss of profits, revenue, or business interruption.</p>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, SiteTrack’s total cumulative liability for any direct damages arising out of or relating to this Agreement shall be limited to the total amount of subscription fees actually paid by the Customer to SiteTrack in the twelve (12) months immediately preceding the event giving rise to the claim. <strong>Exceptions:</strong> This liability cap does not apply to claims arising from either party's fraud, wilful misconduct, gross negligence, intellectual property infringement, or breaches of confidentiality.</p>

    <h2>8. TERM, TERMINATION & DATA EXPORT</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Termination:</span> Either party may terminate this Agreement by providing thirty (30) days written notice, or immediately for a material breach that is not cured within 14 days of notice.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Data Export:</span> Upon termination, the Customer will have a period of thirty (30) days to export their Customer Data in standard formats (e.g., CSV and PDF reports), after which SiteTrack may permanently delete all associated data.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>9. GENERAL PROVISIONS</h2>
    <ol>
        <li><span class="clause">Modifications:</span> SiteTrack may modify these Terms by providing at least 30 days prior written notice. Continued use of the Service after such notice constitutes acceptance of the modified Terms.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Assignment:</span> Neither party may assign this Agreement without the prior written consent of the other party, except in the case of a merger or acquisition.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Notices:</span> Legal notices must be sent in writing to [Insert Legal Contact Email] for SiteTrack, and to the primary administrator email on file for the Customer.</li>
        <li><span class="clause">Governing Law:</span> This Agreement is governed by the laws of [Insert State, e.g., Victoria/New South Wales], Australia.</li>
    </ol>

